Keep SSE2 for LtHash's scalar fallback on QNX x86_64.

MathOperation_Simple.cpp is compiled with -mno-avx -mno-avx2 -mno-sse2 to
get a plain scalar variant. With x87 arithmetic GCC reports
__FLT_EVAL_METHOD__ as -1 in C++, a value for which QNX's <math.h> declares
no double_t or float_t, and libc++'s <cmath> fails ('double_t' has not been
declared). On QNX the file keeps SSE2 (the x86-64 baseline) and loses only
AVX: the code is the same scalar code, possibly vectorised by the compiler.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/folly/crypto/detail/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/folly/crypto/detail/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -31,13 +31,16 @@
 )
 
 # Apply SSE2/AVX2 compile flags on x86
+# Not -mno-sse2 on QNX: x87 arithmetic makes GCC report __FLT_EVAL_METHOD__
+# -1 in C++, for which QNX's <math.h> declares no double_t/float_t, and
+# libc++'s <cmath> then fails to compile.
 if (IS_X86_64_ARCH)
   target_compile_options(
     folly_crypto_detail_math_operation_simple_obj
     PRIVATE
       -mno-avx
       -mno-avx2
-      -mno-sse2
+      $<$<NOT:$<STREQUAL:${CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME},QNX>>:-mno-sse2>
   )
 endif ()
 
